/* ================================================================================ */
/* Test 1: Index Creation and Basic Operations */
/* ================================================================================ */
"Test 1: Index Creation and Basic Operations\n".echo();
"-------------------------------------------\n".echo();

"Understanding index creation process:\n".echo();
"1. Create index on specified fields\n".echo();
"2. Index automatically populated with existing data\n".echo();
"3. Index enables fast searching on indexed fields\n".echo();

"Index creation workflow:\n".echo();
"```cpp\n".echo();
" /* Create index on specified fields\n".echo(); */
"GrapaDBIndex dbIndex;\n".echo();
"GrapaDU64Array fieldList(2);\n".echo();
"fieldList.Append(1, nameFieldId);\n".echo();
"fieldList.Append(2, ageFieldId);\n".echo();
"err = CreateIndex(table, indexId, fieldList, dbIndex);\n".echo();
"```\n".echo();

/* ================================================================================ */
/* Test 2: Index Field Addition */
/* ================================================================================ */
"Test 2: Index Field Addition\n".echo();
"----------------------------\n".echo();

"Understanding index field addition:\n".echo();
"Process: Add field to existing index definition and rebuild entire index\n".echo();

"Implementation details:\n".echo();
"```cpp\n".echo();
" /* Adding a field to an existing index\n".echo(); */
"GrapaError GrapaDB::CreateIndexField(GrapaDBIndex& pIndex, u64 pIndexFieldId, u64 pFieldId)\n".echo();
"{\n".echo();
" /* Add field to index definition\n".echo(); */
"    indexCursor.Set(indexFieldsRef, SU64_ITEM, pIndexFieldId, pFieldId);\n".echo();
"    err = Insert(indexCursor);\n".echo();
"    \n".echo();
" /* Rebuild entire index with new field\n".echo(); */
"    indexCursor.Set(pIndex.mRef, TREE_ITEM);\n".echo();
"    EmptyTree(indexCursor); /* Clear existing index data\n".echo(); */
"    dtCursor.Set(pIndex.mTable.mRef);\n".echo();
"    err = First(dtCursor);\n".echo();
"    while(!err) {\n".echo();
" /* Rebuild index entries for all records\n".echo(); */
"        indexCursor.Set(pIndex.mRef, RPTR_ITEM, dtCursor.mKey);\n".echo();
"        Insert(indexCursor);\n".echo();
"        err = Next(dtCursor);\n".echo();
"    }\n".echo();
"    return(0);\n".echo();
"}\n".echo();
"```\n".echo();

/* ================================================================================ */
/* Test 3: Index Refresh Process */
/* ================================================================================ */
"Test 3: Index Refresh Process\n".echo();
"-----------------------------\n".echo();

"Understanding index refresh (complete rebuild):\n".echo();
"Process: Clear all index data and rebuild from scratch\n".echo();

"Implementation details:\n".echo();
"```cpp\n".echo();
" /* Complete index rebuild\n".echo(); */
"GrapaError GrapaDB::RefreshIndex(GrapaDBIndex& pIndex)\n".echo();
"{\n".echo();
"    GrapaCursor indexCursor, dtCursor;\n".echo();
"    indexCursor.Set(pIndex.mRef);\n".echo();
"    EmptyTree(indexCursor); /* Clear all index data\n".echo(); */
"    \n".echo();
"    dtCursor.Set(pIndex.mTable.mRef);\n".echo();
"    err = First(dtCursor);\n".echo();
"    while(!err) {\n".echo();
" /* Rebuild index entries for all records\n".echo(); */
"        indexCursor.Set(pIndex.mRef, RPTR_ITEM, dtCursor.mKey, dtCursor.mValue);\n".echo();
"        Insert(indexCursor);\n".echo();
"        err = Next(dtCursor);\n".echo();
"    }\n".echo();
"    return(0);\n".echo();
"}\n".echo();
"```\n".echo();

/* ================================================================================ */
/* Test 4: Delete-and-Recreate Strategy */
/* ================================================================================ */
"Test 4: Delete-and-Recreate Strategy\n".echo();
"------------------------------------\n".echo();

"Understanding the delete-and-recreate approach:\n".echo();

"Index Modification Workflow:\n".echo();
"1. Delete Index: Remove existing index completely\n".echo();
"2. Create New Index: Create index with updated field list\n".echo();
"3. Rebuild Data: Index is automatically populated with all existing records\n".echo();
"4. Atomic Operation: Index changes are atomic - either complete or not at all\n".echo();

"Advantages of Delete-and-Recreate:\n".echo();
"- Simplicity: No complex index modification logic to maintain\n".echo();
"- Reliability: Eliminates edge cases in index modification\n".echo();
"- Consistency: Ensures index is always in a consistent state\n".echo();
"- Performance: Rebuilding is often faster than complex modifications\n".echo();
"- Debugging: Easier to debug and verify index integrity\n".echo();

"Implementation:\n".echo();
"```cpp\n".echo();
" /* Delete existing index\n".echo(); */
"err = DeleteIndex(table, oldIndexId);\n".echo();
"\n".echo();
" /* Create new index with updated definition\n".echo(); */
"GrapaDBIndex newIndex;\n".echo();
"GrapaDU64Array newFieldList(3);\n".echo();
"newFieldList.Append(1, nameFieldId);\n".echo();
"newFieldList.Append(2, ageFieldId);\n".echo();
"newFieldList.Append(3, departmentFieldId); /* Added field\n".echo(); */
"err = CreateIndex(table, newIndexId, newFieldList, newIndex);\n".echo();
"```\n".echo();

/* ================================================================================ */
/* Test 5: When to Use Each Approach */
/* ================================================================================ */
"Test 5: When to Use Each Approach\n".echo();
"---------------------------------\n".echo();

"Guidelines for index management:\n".echo();

"Field Addition:\n".echo();
"- Use `CreateIndexField()` for adding fields to existing indexes\n".echo();
"- Index is automatically rebuilt with new field\n".echo();
"- Preserves existing index ID and metadata\n".echo();

"Field Removal:\n".echo();
"- Delete and recreate index with new field list\n".echo();
"- Cannot remove individual fields from existing index\n".echo();
"- Ensures clean index state\n".echo();

"Index Type Changes:\n".echo();
"- Delete and recreate with new index type\n".echo();
"- May require different storage or comparison logic\n".echo();
"- Complete index rebuild ensures consistency\n".echo();

"Bulk Changes:\n".echo();
"- Delete and recreate for multiple field changes\n".echo();
"- More efficient than multiple incremental changes\n".echo();
"- Atomic operation ensures data consistency\n".echo();

/* ================================================================================ */
/* Test 6: Implementation Considerations */
/* ================================================================================ */
"Test 6: Implementation Considerations\n".echo();
"------------------------------------\n".echo();

"Important considerations for index management:\n".echo();

"Transaction Safety:\n".echo();
"- Index operations should be wrapped in transactions\n".echo();
"- Ensures atomicity of index changes\n".echo();
"- Provides rollback capability on failure\n".echo();

"Performance:\n".echo();
"- Large tables may require background index rebuilding\n".echo();
"- Consider impact on query performance during rebuild\n".echo();
"- May need to disable indexes during bulk operations\n".echo();

"Availability:\n".echo();
"- Consider index rebuilding impact on query performance\n".echo();
"- May need to maintain multiple index versions\n".echo();
"- Plan for index maintenance windows\n".echo();

"Recovery:\n".echo();
"- Maintain ability to rollback index changes\n".echo();
"- Keep backup of index definitions\n".echo();
"- Monitor index integrity after changes\n".echo();

/* ================================================================================ */
/* Test 7: Index Management Summary */
/* ================================================================================ */
"Test 7: Index Management Summary\n".echo();
"--------------------------------\n".echo();

"Current index operations available:\n".echo();
"1. Create Index: group_db.mkindex(indexId, fieldList) - Create new index\n".echo();
"2. Delete Index: group_db.delindex(indexId) - Remove index completely\n".echo();
"3. Refresh Index: group_db.refreshindex(indexId) - Rebuild index from scratch\n".echo();
"4. Add Index Field: group_db.addindexfield(indexId, fieldId) - Add field to index\n".echo();

"Index Management Philosophy:\n".echo();
"- Simple and reliable operations\n".echo();
"- Delete-and-recreate for complex changes\n".echo();
"- Atomic operations ensure consistency\n".echo();
"- Prioritize data integrity over optimization\n".echo();

"Alignment with Database File System Vision:\n".echo();
"- Operations are simple, reliable, and atomic\n".echo();
"- Similar to file system operations (delete file, create new file)\n".echo();
"- Prioritizes system reliability and maintainability\n".echo();
"- Eliminates complex edge cases and corruption risks\n".echo();

/* ================================================================================ */
/* Test 8: Demonstrate Index Usage */
/* ================================================================================ */
"Test 8: Demonstrate Index Usage\n".echo();
"-------------------------------\n".echo();

"Understanding how indexes improve search performance:\n".echo();

"Without Index (Sequential Scan):\n".echo();
"- Scan all records in table\n".echo();
"- Compare each record against search criteria\n".echo();
"- Performance: O(n) where n = number of records\n".echo();

"With Index (Indexed Search):\n".echo();
"- Use index to find relevant record range\n".echo();
"- Only scan records within that range\n".echo();
"- Performance: O(log n) for index lookup + O(k) for range scan\n".echo();

"Two-Stage Search Algorithm:\n".echo();
"1. Stage 1: Locate best index and constrain cursor to index range\n".echo();
"2. Stage 2: Detailed field matching within the constrained range\n".echo();

"Index Selection Process:\n".echo();
"- Scan available indexes for search fields\n".echo();
"- Choose index that covers most search criteria\n".echo();
"- Fall back to sequential scan if no suitable index\n".echo();

